title: The American Crossing to Cuba
tags: event
view-if: war_stage = 1 and invasion_force_strength > 0
face-image: img/Tr great white fleet from photo nh100349 USS Connecticut 1907.jpg

= Crossing the Florida Strait

Weeks of preparation have brought the expedition to Florida's southern coast. Thousands of American soldiers board crowded transports as naval officers make final inspections and supply crews load the last provisions. Crowds gather along the docks to watch the fleet depart.

Escorted by the United States Navy, the American Expeditionary Force heads across the Florida Strait toward Cuba. For many of the soldiers aboard, this will be their first combat. Families across the country wait for news of those sailing south.

God bless the troops.

- @Transport: Begin the Crossing

@Transport
go-to: Battle

@Battle

= Spanish Vessels Appear

The invasion fleet steams south under clear skies. American warships screen the transports as the Cuban coast comes into view.

Then the lookouts spot smoke to the east.

Spanish warships are approaching the convoy, attempting to stop the invasion before the American army can reach Cuba. Signal flags go up across the fleet as guns are loaded and crews take their positions.

- @Fight: Engage the Spanish Fleet!
- @Retreat: Order a Retreat

@Fight
subtitle: Defeat the Spanish Navy and secure the crossing.
on-arrival: {!

    let american_strength = Q.navy_strength * (1.0 + (Q.navy_loyalty * 0.05));

    if (american_strength > Q.spain_navy_strength) {
        Q.battle_keys_outcome = "victory";
        Q.war_stage += 1;
        Q.navy_strength *= 0.95;
        Q.navy_loyalty *= 1.05;
    } else {
        Q.battle_keys_outcome = "defeat";
        Q.navy_strength *= 0.75;
        Q.navy_loyalty *= 0.75;
    }

!}
go-to: Victory if battle_keys_outcome = "victory"; Defeat if battle_keys_outcome = "defeat"

@Retreat
subtitle: Abandon the invasion.
on-arrival: spain_war = 0
go-to: Defeat

@Victory

= VICTORY

The fleets exchange fire in what newspapers will soon call the Battle of the Florida Strait. American gunnery and maneuvering give the United States the advantage. Several Spanish vessels are sunk or driven ashore while the remainder retreat toward Havana.

- @Continue: Continue

@Continue

The war rages on...